,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,2,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,2,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,2,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,2,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7]],"output":[[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,2,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,2,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,2,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,2,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,2,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7]]}]},"teaching_variant":"canonical","teacher_models":["claude-opus-5-5"],"explanation":"## How the puzzle works\n\n**What the grid contains.** Each grid is a plain background (colour 7) with one short diagonal line of colour 2. The line runs from lower-left to upper-right, one cell per step.\n\n**What changes.** Comparing the three train pairs:\n\n| pair | input line (bottom → top) | length | output line (bottom → top) | length |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2 | (15,0) | 1 | (14,1),(13,2) | 2 |\n| 1 | (14,1),(13,2) | 2 | (12,3),(11,4),(10,5) | 3 |\n| 3 | (12,3),(11,4),(10,5) | 3 | (9,6),(8,7),(7,8),(6,9) | 4 |\n\nThe pairs form a chain: each output is the next pair's input. In every pair:\n- The old line is erased; every 2 becomes 7 in the fact sheet.\n- A new line appears one length longer.\n- The new line starts at the cell diagonally up-right of the old top end and continues up-right.\n\nSo the line \"hops forward\" along its own diagonal and grows by one cell each step.\n\n**Rule.**\n1. Collect the coloured cells.\n2. Find the top-right end (smallest y), its colour, and the count n.\n3. Blank all the coloured cells to background.\n4. Draw n+1 cells starting at (top_y−1, top_x+1), stepping (−1,+1). Clip at the grid edge.\n\nThe direction (up-right) is the same in every pair, so it is a fixed constant. The background, the colour and the length are all read from the grid.\n\n**Test input.** The line is (9,6),(8,7),(7,8),(6,9), length 4, top end (6,9). It is erased. A 5-cell line is drawn at (5,10),(4,11),(3,12),(2,13),(1,14). All five cells fit inside the 16×16 grid.\n\n**Teaching stages.** Two edits are recorded with `emit`:\n1. The old line erased (an empty canvas).\n2. The longer line drawn in its new position (the final grid).","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    cells = [(int(y), int(x)) for y, x in zip(*np.nonzero(g != bg))]\n    out = g.copy()\n    if not cells:\n        emit(out, \"No line found; nothing to do.\")\n        return out\n    n = len(cells)\n    ty, tx = min(cells)  # top end of the up-right diagonal (smallest y)\n    col = int(g[ty, tx])\n    for y, x in cells:\n        out[y, x] = bg\n    emit(out, f\"Erase the old diagonal line of {n} cells.\")\n    H, W = out.shape\n    for k in range(1, n + 2):\n        y, x = ty - k, tx + k\n        if 0 <= y < H and 0 <= x < W:\n            out[y, x] = col\n    emit(out, f\"Draw a {n+1}-cell line continuing up-right from just past the old top end.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Find the top-right end (smallest y), its colour, and the count n."}],"count":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Find the top-right end (smallest y), its colour, and the count n."}],"scale":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The line runs from lower-left to upper-right, one cell per step."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"a4ad244d374cd87a9210bd0193b87597220e8ef27f599a8fc5f908cdef60759d","task_sha256":"d152b539c1e18534d2f4e8ac4e5d415c8081916ada9ff9442217df4ff3848748","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
